<BaseLayout
  title="Category comparison"
  description="A dated, source-first comparison of Restless and adjacent agent products."
  active="compare"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>Close neighbours.<br /><em>Different centre.</em></h1>
    <p>These are public positioning observations checked on 26 August 2026. The interpretation is ours. It is not a feature benchmark or a claim that one product is better.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="comparison-list" aria-label="Source-first category comparison">
    <article><h2>opencompany</h2><p>Its public site presents an open-source multiplayer AI workspace with connected sources, workflows, multiple agent harnesses and cloud sandboxes.</p><p><strong>Observed centre:</strong> a shared workspace where people and agents run company processes together.</p><a href="https://www.opencompany.cloud/" rel="noreferrer">Open primary source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    <article><h2>Lindy</h2><p>Its public site presents an AI teammate that connects to company tools and takes work across those tools. Its product pages also foreground scheduled jobs and integrations.</p><p><strong>Observed centre:</strong> a connected AI teammate that runs work in the channels a team already uses.</p><a href="https://www.lindy.ai/" rel="noreferrer">Open primary source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    <article><h2>CrewAI</h2><p>Its documentation presents a developer framework for collaborative agents, crews and event-driven flows with structured control.</p><p><strong>Observed centre:</strong> developer-defined multi-agent applications and orchestration.</p><a href="https://docs.crewai.com/index" rel="noreferrer">Open primary source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    <article class="restless-comparison"><h2>Restless</h2><p>Restless is aiming at an owner/operator who delegates a whole economic outcome and receives the prepared last mile. Its product research focuses on accountable leads, persistent work and governed effects.</p><p><strong>Intended centre:</strong> useful company output per unit of scarce owner attention.</p><a href="/product/">Read the product boundary <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
  </section>

  <section class="paired-prose">
    <h2>The difference is where the owner stands.</h2>
    <div><p>Restless is not centred on a workspace to inhabit, a toolkit to configure or a workflow definition to build. The intended experience is one accountable company that handles the surrounding work and returns the decision only its owner can make.</p><p>Public materials change. This comparison preserves its date and sources so it can be corrected rather than treated as a permanent market fact.</p></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
